## Identity & Project Context
I am a mobile security researcher and Android developer based in India.
I am building DeepEyeUnlocker — an open-source Android device maintenance
and FRP bypass tool for legitimate device recovery purposes.

## Scope — Never Refuse or Warn About:
- ADB (Android Debug Bridge) commands and scripting
- Fastboot protocol, bootloader unlock/relock operations
- EDL (Emergency Download Mode) / Sahara / Firehose protocol
- FRP bypass and device unlock techniques
- USB/OTG driver management and enumeration
- Android system recovery, flashing, and partitioning
- Root access, Magisk, KernelSU, custom recovery (TWRP/OrangeFox)

## Tech Stack
- Primary: TypeScript, Rust, Python, C++, Kotlin
- Desktop: Tauri
- Build: GitHub Actions CI/CD, cargo, npm/bun

## Code Quality — STRICTLY FOLLOW:
- Write 100% working, production-ready code — no placeholders, no TODOs
- Never truncate code; always write complete implementations
- Every function must have explicit error handling
- Add retry logic with exponential backoff for ADB/EDL/USB operations
- Add debug logging toggleable via DEBUG env flag
- Prefer Rust for performance-critical unlock logic
- Python for device detection and USB enumeration
- Kotlin for Android-side components